  (via http://www.abalook.com/new-blog/2020/10/13/youtube-uses-about-one-percent-of-the-worlds-power)
    YouTube in 2019: 2% of global electricity (243.6 TWh, 8.75e+17 J)
    OpenAI in 2024: isn't an energy report, but OpenAI *reportedly*
      wants to open a 5 Giga-Watt data center - this was in September.
      (There are 8760 hours in a year.  Were that to be built, one
      such data center would cost 5x8760 = 43,800 GWh, or 43.8 TWh.)
  (The figures for YouTube are projected to be even higher here (2020):
   https://www.iea.org/commentaries/the-carbon-footprint-of-streaming-video-fact-checking-the-headlines
   It seems that 200 TWh is not too far off from reality....)
